WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.939 --> 00:00:15.783
don't get this," Will Jacobs grumbled as he tried to do his fourth-grade science homework.

2
00:00:16.603 --> 00:00:20.646
His mother stepped into the doorway and asked, "Will, are you done with your homework?

3
00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:22.207
It's almost time for bed."

4
00:00:22.227 --> 00:00:26.130
"No. I'm still trying to answer these questions.

5
00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:28.772
I just don't understand earthquakes.

6
00:00:29.332 --> 00:00:30.712
How can the earth shake?"

7
00:00:30.732 --> 00:00:33.673
"Why don't you take a little break?"

8
00:00:34.253 --> 00:00:35.334
Will's mom suggested.

9
00:00:35.354 --> 00:00:36.874
"That sometimes helps."

10
00:00:39.915 --> 00:00:42.776
After his mom left, Will set an alarm on his phone.

11
00:00:43.776 --> 00:00:46.737
He had just gotten it for his birthday, and he loved the new gadget.

12
00:00:47.097 --> 00:00:49.898
Will put his head down on the desk and instantly fell asleep.

13
00:00:51.498 --> 00:00:54.279
Soon the alarm went off, making the table vibrate.

14
00:00:54.859 --> 00:00:58.720
Will silenced it, ignoring the message on the phone's screen: "WAKE UP!"

15
00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:03.942
He went back to sleep, only to be woken up again by another vibration.

16
00:01:04.963 --> 00:01:10.245
But this time when Will opened his eyes, he wasn't in his room—he was in a dark, long

17
00:01:10.346 --> 00:01:14.148
cave. And the phone wasn't vibrating—the ground was shaking!

18
00:01:14.168 --> 00:01:17.870
"Whoa," thought Will.

19
00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:19.350
"What's going on?"

20
00:01:20.891 --> 00:01:22.932
A voice nearby squeaked, "Alert!

21
00:01:23.353 --> 00:01:26.794
Earthquake!" Will looked around but didn't see anyone.

22
00:01:27.235 --> 00:01:29.416
Then he spotted a patch of light on the ground.

23
00:01:30.432 --> 00:01:32.453
He looked closer and saw that it was his phone.

24
00:01:32.993 --> 00:01:34.354
The voice came from the device!

25
00:01:35.974 --> 00:01:39.756
Will picked up the phone, mumbling to himself, "This is strange.

26
00:01:40.496 --> 00:01:41.577
Phones can't talk!"

27
00:01:42.857 --> 00:01:47.579
"Most phones don't talk, but I am a QT-9000."

28
00:01:47.899 --> 00:01:50.040
He almost dropped it again when the phone replied!

29
00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.261
"I can talk and do much more.

30
00:01:53.861 --> 00:01:56.202
I'm the smartest phone you'll ever have!

31
00:01:56.803 --> 00:01:58.223
You can call me QT."

32
00:01:58.243 --> 00:02:01.180
"Wow!" Will exclaimed.

33
00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.961
"Can you tell me what's happening?

34
00:02:03.601 --> 00:02:04.241
Where am I?"

35
00:02:04.261 --> 00:02:08.342
"My sensors indicate that we are in a cave.

36
00:02:08.742 --> 00:02:12.883
And we just experienced a small earthquake," replied QT.

37
00:02:14.744 --> 00:02:16.945
All of a sudden, the ground started shaking again.

38
00:02:16.965 --> 00:02:22.886
"And this is a big earthquake," QT said as a whole section of the rock wall moved.

39
00:02:24.067 --> 00:02:26.447
Will noticed light coming through a crack in the ceiling.

40
00:02:26.467 --> 00:02:31.429
"I'm getting out of here," he said, stuffing the phone in his pocket.

41
00:02:31.990 --> 00:02:33.271
He climbed out to the surface.

42
00:02:36.853 --> 00:02:38.894
Nearby a road had torn in half.

43
00:02:39.555 --> 00:02:44.358
Will pulled his phone out and asked, "How can a huge part of the ground move like that?"

44
00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.040
A map of the world appeared on QT's screen.

45
00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:54.324
"The surface of the planet, called the crust, is made up of chunks called tectonic plates.

46
00:02:55.776 --> 00:03:01.098
There are 12 large plates and many smaller ones," QT explained.

47
00:03:01.118 --> 00:03:08.380
"The plates float on top of the mantle, a soft layer of rock and other materials.

48
00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:14.061
Underneath the mantle is a layer of liquid metal called the outer core.

49
00:03:14.681 --> 00:03:18.863
And underneath that is the inner core, which is solid metal.

50
00:03:20.643 --> 00:03:26.674
It's very hot at the center of the planet, and the heat escaping from there makes the plates

51
00:03:26.774 --> 00:03:31.657
move. The movement is what causes earthquakes," said QT.

52
00:03:33.598 --> 00:03:40.262
"Oh Will thought for a moment and then asked, "If the plates are constantly moving, why aren't earthquakes

53
00:03:40.302 --> 00:03:41.482
happening all the time?"

54
00:03:41.502 --> 00:03:44.404
"Actually they are!

55
00:03:45.064 --> 00:03:48.186
Most are just so small that people don't feel them.

56
00:03:49.307 --> 00:03:55.515
Big earthquakes, like this one, happen when friction stops the edges of the plates from moving for a

57
00:03:55.576 --> 00:04:02.461
while. When they finally break loose, they release all that stored energy, like a spring."

58
00:04:03.402 --> 00:04:04.763
QT paused for a second.

59
00:04:04.783 --> 00:04:10.348
"My GPS tells me that we are on the San Andreas Fault, in California."

60
00:04:11.649 --> 00:04:12.770
Will's eyes lit up.

61
00:04:12.790 --> 00:04:15.452
"We learned about faults in science class!

62
00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:19.556
A fault is the crack between two plates in the planet's crust!"

63
00:04:20.768 --> 00:04:21.989
Will looked at the road again.

64
00:04:22.009 --> 00:04:24.010
"That must be a fault over there."

65
00:04:24.030 --> 00:04:26.392
"Yes, it is.

66
00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:31.896
Two plates are sliding past each other here, causing powerful earthquakes.

67
00:04:33.177 --> 00:04:35.619
Faults also often appear by mountains.

68
00:04:36.419 --> 00:04:42.103
That's because when two plates come together, their edges can wrinkle and fold to make mountains."

69
00:04:42.844 --> 00:04:43.964
Will scratched his head.

70
00:04:43.984 --> 00:04:46.366
"What happens when plates move apart?

71
00:04:46.926 --> 00:04:48.828
Do huge holes appear in the ground?"

72
00:04:50.596 --> 00:04:56.280
"No. Right now the places where plates are moving apart are mostly under the ocean.

73
00:04:57.361 --> 00:05:02.845
Down there magma—that's hot, liquid rock—rises from between the plates.

74
00:05:04.226 --> 00:05:10.411
It cools when it touches the cold water, so it hardens and becomes part of the crust," QT

75
00:05:10.451 --> 00:05:14.234
explained. "Earthquakes can be very destructive.

76
00:05:15.234 --> 00:05:21.089
If that road over there is destroyed, just imagine what can happen in a city during an earthquake.

77
00:05:21.629 --> 00:05:23.230
Actually I'll show you."

78
00:05:24.310 --> 00:05:27.671
"How? We're nowhere near a city," Will pointed out.

79
00:05:28.911 --> 00:05:31.012
"Look at my screen and I'll transport us.

80
00:05:31.532 --> 00:05:33.432
I told you I have special skills."

81
00:05:34.553 --> 00:05:37.574
Will gazed down at the screen and saw a street in ruins.

82
00:05:38.194 --> 00:05:39.594
Then everything got dark.

83
00:05:41.355 --> 00:05:43.775
A moment later Will found himself in the city!

84
00:05:44.256 --> 00:05:45.796
He was standing in a crowded park.

85
00:05:47.296 --> 00:05:49.837
Will was shocked by the destruction around him.

86
00:05:49.857 --> 00:05:53.438
"I'd better stay here, away from the buildings.

87
00:05:54.658 --> 00:06:00.380
My science teacher said that aftershocks always come after a big earthquake, but we don't know when.

88
00:06:01.620 --> 00:06:04.701
It's dangerous because more parts of the buildings could fall.

89
00:06:05.241 --> 00:06:06.042
But where are we?"

90
00:06:06.642 --> 00:06:07.182
asked Will.

91
00:06:07.202 --> 00:06:14.364
"This is San Francisco after a magnitude 6.9 earthquake," QT replied.

92
00:06:15.836 --> 00:06:21.961
"The earthquake's epicenter was actually about a hundred kilometers away, but you can see how much power it

93
00:06:22.001 --> 00:06:24.983
released." Will looked confused.

94
00:06:25.583 --> 00:06:29.026
"What's an epicenter, and what does magnitude mean?"

95
00:06:29.046 --> 00:06:33.029
"Earthquakes start deep underground.

96
00:06:33.489 --> 00:06:37.993
The spot on the surface of the planet above the earthquake is called its epicenter.

97
00:06:39.934 --> 00:06:42.416
Magnitude is the strength of an earthquake.

98
00:06:44.284 --> 00:06:50.949
Each point on the magnitude scale is ten times stronger than the one before, so an 8-point earthquake

99
00:06:51.069 --> 00:06:53.631
is ten times stronger than a 7-point.

100
00:06:55.192 --> 00:06:58.395
Can you imagine damage ten times worse than this?"

101
00:06:59.636 --> 00:07:00.516
Will shook his head.

102
00:07:00.536 --> 00:07:03.158
"No. This is pretty bad.

103
00:07:03.658 --> 00:07:05.019
How do they measure magnitude?

104
00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:07.341
Do they count the buildings that fell or something?"

105
00:07:08.642 --> 00:07:10.804
A jagged line appeared on QT's screen.

106
00:07:11.392 --> 00:07:14.755
"People who study earthquakes are called seismologists.

107
00:07:15.816 --> 00:07:21.621
They measure earthquakes with machines called seismographs, which monitor the vibrations in the ground.

108
00:07:22.982 --> 00:07:28.747
Usually the earth doesn't move much, so the waves the seismographs draw are pretty small.

109
00:07:29.828 --> 00:07:33.310
But during an earthquake, the waves get really big.

110
00:07:33.651 --> 00:07:36.313
The size of the waves determines the magnitude."

111
00:07:37.874 --> 00:07:39.676
Suddenly the aftershock came.

112
00:07:40.328 --> 00:07:41.989
The ground rumbled and then moved.

113
00:07:42.649 --> 00:07:44.329
Terrified, Will shut his eyes.

114
00:07:45.550 --> 00:07:48.391
When the sound passed, he slowly opened his eyes.

115
00:07:48.871 --> 00:07:50.931
To his amazement he was back in his room.

116
00:07:51.992 --> 00:07:55.033
His phone was vibrating in his hand; the alarm was going off.

117
00:07:55.053 --> 00:07:59.414
"That was a strange dream he muttered, reaching for his pencil.

118
00:07:59.434 --> 00:08:02.015
"But QT sure is cool!

119
00:08:02.575 --> 00:08:05.516
And now these homework questions will be a piece of cake!"
